                <pb facs="1086" n="966" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg966"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">853.84/12: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Portugal</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Magruder</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lisbon</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-07-07T14:00:00+01:00">July 7, 1931—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 7—12:05 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>21. Decree of July 1st extends national treatment in respect of maritime and port
                    dues to foreign merchant vessels but creates new tonnage dues of one escudo per
                    gross registered ton thereby discriminating against all vessels other than those
                    discharging or loading full cargoes to the manifest advantage of Portuguese
                    bottoms. Text by mail.<anchor n="5" xml:id="d1042-f1"/> Please inform
                    Commerce.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Magruder</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
